SWEET WLAN root port bus master (patch 0160, plan 2026-11-14 oneshot-2 step W7, second iteration; docs/research/51 U8). Run o5-w7-l8 (patch 0159) set up the
rings and switched the endpoint's Bus Master on, but the firmware never fetched a request from host memory ("h2d w 2 fw r 0", completion ring untouched). The
root port forwards the endpoint's memory requests upstream only while its own Command register has Bus Master Enable; Linux sets it on every bridge above an
enabled device (drivers/pci/pci.c:2071-2090, v6.18), and the shim's link bring-up never writes that register. Level 8 now reads and prints the root port's
Command/Status word (RC-local DBI 0x04, no TLP), adds the memory and master bits before the endpoint's Bus Master store, and puts the word back after the
endpoint's Bus Master is off; a stop restores the endpoint first, then the root port. New space SWW_DBI: one readable and writable word, only at level 8.
The value is derived in swl_wr() from the word read (on: old | 0x6; off: the recorded old word), the Status half is written as 0. Glue: the DBI page is mapped
only at level 8; sw3_wr() lets only that word through, only after the release, only if no bit other than memory/master differs from the live word, and the
master bit only with a host pool. Levels 1..7 are unchanged.
Review 0160-1 A1: after each bounded completion wait (pass and stop path) run F prints the endpoint's cfg 0x04 and the root port's DBI 0x04 word once (reads only), so
a second failure shows whether Received Master Abort (Status bit 29) is set.

